 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Only two of the 24 failures are independent of the `set_cookie` `partitioned` TypeError, and a third did not reproduce. I should correct my earlier list: `test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` is a `set_cookie` failure after all.\n\n**Not caused by the `partitioned` TypeError**\n\n1. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**\n   - It fails with `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views` (raised at `src/tessel/app.py:1096`).\n   - The optional async dependency is not installed in this environment.\n\n2. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**\n   - It fails with `assert None == 500000` (`tests/test_request.py:33`).\n   - The installed Werkzeug's `Request` has no `max_form_memory_size` attribute. This is the same older-Werkzeug mismatch as the main cause, but a different symptom.\n\n**Not reproducible**\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**\n   - It failed in the full run with a pytest error, but passed when re-run in isolation.\n   - It is likely order-dependent or flaky, and no root cause was found.\n\n**Caused by the TypeError after all**\n\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` shows an `AssertionError` on the response body, but the log shows a 500 from the `set_cookie` TypeError.\n- The teardown error for `test_stream_keeps_session` is a leftover app context from that test crashing mid-request.\n\nUpgrading Werkzeug would probably fix the main failures and `test_limit_config`. `test_async_view` needs the async extra installed, and the flaky `test_open_resource_exceptions[a]` needs separate investigation.",
